      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes a mechanism that records file state before the guarded write tool executor overwrites any file. Here\u0027s what it does:\n\n**Core function**: Before making any write, the system journals the prior state of that file \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it did not exist.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If the agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order \u2014 restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created ones.\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics**: This gives each run atomic write semantics without requiring a database transaction; the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log for the duration of that single run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback path, since it has no write tool at all \u2014 the journal exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually perform writes.",
